This adds mmvq_multi_parity, built with STRATA_ENABLE_CUDA alone and registered with add_test:

the same Q8_1 bytes through one T-column call and T single-column calls, compared bit for bit, for 7 cases (Q4_0, Q8_0, Q4_K, Q5_K, Q6_K, IQ4_XS, a wide Q5_K) and T = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8;
random weight bytes with each block's fp16 scales rewritten as normal values, so every output is finite: on the GPU every NaN has the same bits, so a NaN output would compare equal whatever produced it. A non-finite output fails the test;
